    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d595">

                <pb facs="1051" n="1037" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1037"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1406: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-22T14:00:00+03:00">April 22, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 23—7:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1395. I informed Vyshinski on April 21 of the contents of the Department’s 937,
                    April 17 and left with him a memorandum on the subject which included a
                    statement inquiring whether the Soviet Government would issue a statement
                    expressing its attitude concerning Nazi atrocities. Vyshinski replied that the
                    Soviet Government had frequently expressed its position on this subject, however
                    he would bring the memorandum to the attention of his Government and give the
                    matter his personal study.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d595-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d595-f1" n="7" xml:id="d595-f1-content">
                <p>Soviet action in this matter was not obtained.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
